            <ArticleTitle>[The activity of mitochondrial enzymes in the myocardium in chronic coronary failure during the administration of antianginal agents].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The experiments with Chinchilla rabbits indicated that the activity of mitochondria-associated enzymes changed hetero-directionally in chronic coronary insufficiency. The activity of creatine kinase changed most greatly. Obsidan and finoptin were found to show a different effect on the activity of the tested enzymes in the cardiac mitochondria during experimental coronary insufficiency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
